# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# mount: /devices/board1
# board: yes
# A store that is attached gets a row; one that is not gets nothing.
#
# This is the row /sys, /dev and /data used to occupy, written into every
# menu whether the machine had them or not.  What is in the menu now is
# what a person can actually reach.
wait 15
click 980 20
wait 4
expect-menu Find…|Force Quit…|Settings|Applications|Device Tools|-|board1|-|Recent folders|-|Shut down…|
note and the row opens the store it names, by the name the namespace
note knows it by rather than by whatever the store calls its own root
menu-pick board1
wait 14
expect-title board1
expect-rows-at-least 2
quit
